@* V1009_CLIENT_START_GUIDE *@
<section class="client-start-guide" aria-labelledby="client-start-title">
    <div class="client-start-guide-head">
        <div>
            <span class="client-start-kicker">YOUR FIRST WEEK</span>
            <h2 id="client-start-title">Learn the system while the system learns your pattern</h2>
        </div>
        <a asp-controller="Home"
           asp-action="Evidence"
           class="client-start-evidence-link">Why the evidence matters</a>
    </div>

    <p class="client-start-lead">Plan, log, and measure for 12 weeks to learn how your body responds.</p>

    <div class="client-start-loop" aria-label="12 Week Recomp daily loop">
        <span>Plan</span>
        <b>&rarr;</b>
        <span>Do</span>
        <b>&rarr;</b>
        <span>Log</span>
        <b>&rarr;</b>
        <span>Measure</span>
        <b>&rarr;</b>
        <span>Learn</span>
        <b>&rarr;</b>
        <span>Adapt</span>
    </div>

    <div class="client-start-grid">
        <div>
            <strong>Weekly Plan = your intention</strong>
            <p>Build a week you can realistically complete.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <strong>Daily Entry = what actually happened</strong>
            <p>Log what you actually trained and ate.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <strong>Morning scale = the next piece of evidence</strong>
            <p>When possible, measure under similar morning conditions. Yesterday's activity and nutrition are interpreted with the next morning's scale response.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <strong>Dashboard = interpretation, not judgment</strong>
            <p>Green, yellow, orange, red, and gray signals help explain the day. One number never tells the whole story.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <strong>Progress = the trend</strong>
            <p>Daily readings fluctuate. Track the trend.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <strong>The goal = skills you keep</strong>
            <p>Use the next 12 weeks to learn how training, food, and recovery work for you.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="client-start-priorities">
        <div><strong>Hard training days</strong> <span>Prioritize protein and carbs for recovery.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Easy cardio and recovery</strong> <span>Prioritize energy balance. Easier days may need fewer carbs.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Logging accuracy</strong> <span>Count portions, cooking fats, sauces, snacks, and drinks.</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="client-start-note"><strong>What success looks like:</strong> consistent training, recovery, accurate logging, and habits you can keep.</div>
</section>